Relevant columns and their possible usage
• airports_data.airport_code – joins each flight to its airport row  
• airports_data.city – JSON with the English city name (json_extract(city,'$.en'))  
• airports_data.coordinates – point '(lon,lat)', supply latitude & longitude that let us compute the great‑circle distance  
• flights.departure_airport – foreign key to the origin airport  
• flights.arrival_airport – foreign key to the destination airport  

Typical conditions that will be used
• Join flights.departure_airport = airports_data.airport_code (origin)  
• Join flights.arrival_airport   = airports_data.airport_code (destination)  
• To make a city pair direction‑free  
        CASE WHEN c1 < c2 THEN (c1,c2) ELSE (c2,c1) END  
• To place an average distance into the requested classes  
        CASE WHEN avg_dist < 1000  THEN '0‑1000'  
